# Platform Admin Tenant list and Tenant suspension (ticket 12).
# Log in as a Platform Admin with http/auth.http (see http/platform-applications.http for creating one).

@baseUrl = http://localhost:9800
@accessToken = paste-platform-admin-access-token
@tenantId = paste-tenant-id

### Every Tenant, newest first (paginated: limit, cursor), with Membership count, enabled
### Application count, creation date and suspendedAt. Nothing from inside the Tenant.
GET {{baseUrl}}/v1/platform/tenants
Authorization: Bearer {{accessToken}}

### Suspend a Tenant (409 if already suspended). Recorded as tenant.suspended in the platform chain.
### From now on: switching into it gets 403, a refresh drops it from the login (the new access token
### has no tid), its Tenant Admin endpoints get 403, and Access Checks deny with tenant-suspended.
POST {{baseUrl}}/v1/platform/tenants/{{tenantId}}/suspend
Authorization: Bearer {{accessToken}}

### Reactivate it (409 if not suspended). Recorded as tenant.reactivated in the platform chain.
POST {{baseUrl}}/v1/platform/tenants/{{tenantId}}/reactivate
Authorization: Bearer {{accessToken}}

### The platform chain shows both events (Platform Admin, no Active Tenant)
GET {{baseUrl}}/v1/platform/audit-events?eventType=tenant.suspended
Authorization: Bearer {{accessToken}}

### A non-admin gets 403 on all of the above
GET {{baseUrl}}/v1/platform/tenants
Authorization: Bearer paste-ordinary-user-access-token
